## .NET Build Artifacts
bin/
obj/
*.user
*.suo
*.cache

## KSA-Bridge runtime config (contains local paths)
ksa-bridge.toml

## IDE
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/

## Node.js
node_modules/
# package-lock.json is committed (standard JS practice for reproducible
# `npm install` / `npm ci`). The lockfile pins exact versions of the
# vendored libs that get copied into examples/*/lib/ via `npm run vendor`.

## Build/deploy scripts and logs
*.log
build_output.txt
build_errors.txt
mqtt_sub_output.txt
mqtt_sub_errors.txt

## Debug & session artifacts
InspectKSA/
InspectTool/
*_debug*.txt
*_inspection*.txt
*_inspection*.log
parent_body_inspection.txt
tool_list.txt

## Temporary helper scripts
download_libs.js
embed_coastlines.js

## Voice models (defensive — KSA-Bridge does not ship voices,
## but a sibling consumer like KSA-PAO might be cloned or symlinked
## here during development. Keep large binary model files out of git.)
*.onnx
*.onnx.json
voices/
models/

## OS metadata
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

## Environment & secrets
.env
.env.*
*.secret

## AI assistant scratch files (Claude / Desktop Commander diagnostic
## wrappers). The `_dc_` prefix marks transient scripts/output dumps
## that helpers spawn for one-off diagnostics. Always disposable.
_dc_*
__cleanup*
